s are not even connected.\" [1330] Nagi told Mizuno, \"Turn them on.\" [1331] Normally, people would turn off the power when they're not using computers. However, the power of Mrs. Hata's computers has been disconnected, which doesn't seem unnatural. But the two workstations are different. This type of computer usually wouldn't have the power disconnected. It's designed to take a long time to start the system, but the machine and system can run continuously for 24 hours. [1332] Suiko touches the switches of the two workstations. Then she plugs in the power cords. Edogawa looks and sees that one of the workstations is from HP, while the other is a domestic product. Although these two workstations are old models from four or five years ago, they would still cost over 10 million yen each to buy. Two of the computers are \"Macintosh\" (Apple computers produced by Apple Inc.), while the other one is unfamiliar and has no markings. It's likely that it was assembled with purchased parts. [1333] Starting the workstations takes a long time. Green English letters and Arabic numbers scroll up from the bottom of the screen. The words \"Red Magic\" appear in red several times. [1334] It takes about a minute to turn on each computer. The display of the unmarked computer stops running after the termination mode turns black. The other computer shows a calendar. The third one stops at the interface of a regular file name. [1335] Edogawa asks, \"Can I touch it? There might be fingerprints on the keyboard\u2026\"\n[1336] \"Ah? Is that so... I've already touched it.\" Mr. Mizuki said while looking at the workstation display, \"Let's extract the fingerprints from the computer over there. Right, Yamanaka? I said I've already touched it.\" [1337] Mr. Yamanaka nodded, \"We have no choice.\" [1338] Ms. Mouri also came to Mr. Sekiguchi's side and touched the computer. The computers were arranged in a radial shape for Ms. Makoto's convenience, so they could only work in a very narrow space. [