n removed. I've longed to see the sea for a long time. Please don't dirty my wedding dress. [1357] Kiri no Uta\n[1358] \"What are these?\" Aragaki Doctor asked, stroking his beard. \"Is this a joke?\" [1359] \"Who are Kazuo Kibito and Kiri no Uta?\" Sawaguchi asked. [1360] Shimano paused for a moment before answering, \"They are the other people existing within Ms. Shinobu Sakurada's body... characters she created herself.\" [1361] \"Why are their names different?\" asked Hikari. [1362] \"How would I know...\" said Yamane. [1363] \"Is it because of different birthplaces...?\" [1364] Dr. Kuwabara replied, \"It's probably that. It's due to different personalities that form the self. Different personalities are inevitably related to different environments. So, generally speaking, different birthplaces or different ages will lead to different personalities. This is a general theory...\"\n[1365] Kishimoto stared at the screen and said, \"In any case, just like Dr. Akigawa warned, she didn't leave any other documents. The files seem to have been sorted out, just like the room.\" [1366] Another folder on the other Apple machine also contained a file with the same content \u2013 \"Read Me.\" [1367] \"There's nothing left here either, except for 'Red Magic' and the new compiler program,\" said S\u0113gawa, glancing at the workstation. \"Has everything else been deleted or moved to a portable hard drive?\" [1368] S\u0113gawa clicked on the information left by the late Dr. Akagi again. \"These two characters should be pronounced 'MICHIRU' (meaning 'flow' in Japanese),\" said M\u00e9nd\u014d, pointing at the screen. Her finger was pointing at the location of the word \"flow\" in the text. [1369] \"Yes, that's right,\" said S\u0113gawa. \"Are you referring to the robot?\" [1370] M\u00e9nd\u014d murmured to herself, \"Or maybe a doll?\" [1371] Wakasa asked, \"What? A doll?\" [1372] Fujimori didn't answer. [1373] After a while, Tsubota started tapping on the keyboard to check the 