hat room with the blue door over there is Kagawa-san's room.\" Ito-san pointed at a T-junction. [2034] Sugawara waved goodbye and headed in that direction. [2035] Miyuki followed Ito-san in the opposite direction. [2036] When Ishta was about to open the door, she handed the files she was holding to Aoi and touched the glass with her right hand. \"I feel a bit inconvenient with this system when I'm holding something in my hand...\"\n[2037] Ishta's room was almost as big as Mounta's room. It had a similar round table and a terminal display, but its position was different from the one in Mounta's room. [2038] The only similarity between the two rooms was that, and everything else was different. One wall of the room was covered with posters of animated films. There were twice as many plastic model robots on the table as the number of \"horses\" in chess (in chess, there are 32 pieces in total, divided into black and white groups, each with 16 pieces. There are two \"horses\" in black and white, making a total of four). They were all painted in bright colors. Aoi couldn't help but associate the bright colors with a festival in Higashino. There were also several cartoon character figurines on the table. A large plastic robot lay on the floor. There was also a 60-centimeter-tall \"Godzilla\" (an iconic monster featured in Japanese science fiction films. \"Godzilla\" was released in 1954 by Toho Company, Ltd., and has since become a pioneer in Japanese monster movies) and a resin monster puppet. Overall, her room was extremely messy. [2039] \"Is it a bit messy?\" Ishta asked apologetically as she turned around, \"Put it over there...?\" [2040] Aoi wondered which way she should go to reach the table. If she walked straight there, she might disturb the things Ishta had arranged. Ishta skillfully navigated through her room like a skilled figure skater, throwing the pile of documents onto the display and turning back. [2041] Momiji finally reached the table and sat down, saying