und and said, \"It's okay.\" She then walked to the edge and looked down. [2407] \"You're really bold,\" said Sukiyama as he lit a cigarette. In reality, it was Mizuki who was outside the fence, not him; he was just very tense. [2408] Mizuki leaped back over the wire fence. \"With a rope, you can go up and down. It's about six or seven meters high...\"\n[2409] \"I couldn't do it,\" said Sukiyama as he exhaled a smoke ring. \"I've always been weak in terms of height.\" [2410] \"I'm the opposite,\" said Mizuki with a smile. \"I like high places.\" [2411] \"Then congratulations to you.\" [2412] \"Teacher, do you have any ideas about what we should investigate next?\" [2413] \"Not yet, let me think\u2026\" Kurosu leaned against the wire fence, smoking. [2414] The air was moist, and people's mood was also very good. The sky in front was pink, and the sound of waves could be heard in the distance. The roof was covered with asphalt waterproofing. The sky below was still dark black. This was the quietest time before dawn. [2415] Suddenly, Kurosu felt as if he was attracted by something. [2416] But he couldn't figure out what it was yet. [2417] Sugita glances at his watch, it's already 4:30 am. He has the habit of checking his watch's second hand every day. But since coming to this island, he hasn't checked it once. It's unnecessary to have an accurate time on this isolated island. The system time inside the computer is not very precise either. The computer also corrects the time every day through the network. [2418] Sugita is very strict about time. He has never been late for class. Generally speaking, students are paying guests, and teachers are the hired ones. Sugita thinks that students can be late, but teachers cannot be late. In fact, he has no special feeling about students who are late. Being late for class and leaving early are both the freedom and rights of students. Teachers have no right to reproach them. [2419] There is a saying that \"time is money.\" Sugita thinks this statement undervalues the value of time. Compared to money, time is worth thousands of times more, and the value of time is equal to the value of life. [2420] Momo is walking back and forth on the empty roof. Although Sugita's gaze follows her, his thoughts have already wandered elsewhere. He is thinking about what he should consider next. [2421] The cigarette in his hand is getting shorter. He puts it on the ground and steps on it to extinguish it. [2422] He decides to look at the list that Hasegawa printed for him. There are about forty A4 pages in total. The first ten pages list the items that have entered or left through the yellow door over the past ten years, including the date, time, whether it was sent in or out, the item name, and the name of the person who confirmed it. The remaining thirty pages record the situation of the items sent by mail. Sugawara quickly scans through them but does not find anything suspicious. All items have been carefully checked. [2423] Large items that enter through the yellow door are mainly mechanical products, work materials, and electrical products, and the packed items have been repackaged. The items sent by mail include daily necessities, books, electronics, consumables, and food. There is also a lot of garbage thrown out of the room. Recently, Dr. Akagi threw out an old set of furniture and some mechanical products. The sent items often contain non-combustible garbage. [2424] Through these, Sugawara has gained a certain understanding of Dr. Akagi's living conditions. He wants to meet the living Dr. Akagi to get a closer look at this extraordinary talent. He came here specifically to meet this genius. How will it be? ... Maybe he will see a talent even stronger than what he imagined. If this is a trick, it should be applauded. If all these things that seem incredible are created by one person, then she must be a genius. [2425] Momiji returns to this place. The sky behind her is already turning white. Her shadow falls on the ground, and her hair shines. [2426] \"Teacher?...\" [2427] \"Good morning,\" Saito said. [2428] Miyuki chuckled. \"Good morning. Have you summarized your thoughts?\" [2429] \"Not yet, still very confused,\" Saito took out a cigarette. [2430] \"I still feel that the information is insufficient,\" Miyuki said, crossing her arms. \"I can only wait for the police investigation.\" [2431] \"But, Matsuriga, we've considered all the possibilities,\" Kurosu said. \"Who the killer is... we'll leave that to the police to investigate... but we saw everything... how did the killer do all of this? It's not a matter of not having enough information. It's a matter of not considering all the angles.\" [2432]3\n[2433] Kurosu and Matsuriga returned to Yamanaka's room. Both terminal devices in the room were turned on, as if Yamanaka were still working. [2434] \"Feel free to use the shower if you'd like,\" Yamanaka said to Kurosu and Matsuriga. \"And if you're hungry, just let me know\u2026\"\n[2435] Kurosu went to the kitchen inside to check the fridge. Matsuriga went to the bathroom to take a shower. After drinking a cup of cold milk, Kurosu returned to the room where Yamanaka was waiting. [2436] \"Oozora went to take a shower,\" Nakajima sat down in a chair next to Yamanaka. \"I drank a cup of milk.\" [2437] \"It's fine,\" Yamanaka didn't stop typing on the keyboard. He looked at Nakajima and said, \"There's an empty room. You can go there and take a nap if you want. There's nothing to eat now...\"\n[2438] \"If Mr. Yamanaka wants something to eat, I can make it for you,\" Nakajima said, lighting a cigarette. \"I can only make scrambled eggs...\"\n[2439] \"Can you make me some?\" Yamanaka smiled at Nakajima's face. \"I'm busy with my work right now. I'm trying the last method.\" [2440] Yamanaka continued to speak to Nakajima while typing on the keyboard. His typing skills were at a level rarely found even in a university. Yamanaka's touch typing had reached a professional l